{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour authoritative-looking doc/comment entry points have drifted from current contracts (audit ae1b). Premises RE-VERIFIED against HEAD 641ba8bed1 — all four still present:\n- **Bare `--assignee <handle>` teaches a Jira-UNRESOLVABLE value.** `README.md:44` (`rebar claim \"$tid\" --assignee alice`) and `README.md:50` (the adjacent library block, `rebar.claim(tid, assignee=\"alice\")`), `docs/user-guide.md:115` (`rebar claim <ticket-id> --assignee alice`), `docs/user-guide.md:234` (`rebar edit <id> --priority=1 --assignee=bob --add-tag=urgent`). Yet `docs/config.md:461-467` documents `ticket.default_assignee` and requires a Jira-resolvable identity — a bare handle is silently cleared by the next reconcile.\n- **MCP navigation mis-route**: `docs/README.md:25` routes \"Drive rebar over MCP\" → `llm-framework.md`, while the complete generated tool reference is `docs/mcp-reference.md` (itself indexed at `docs/README.md:77`).\n- **Removed config surface**: `docs/README.md:91` still describes `config.md` as covering the flat `.rebar/config.conf` keys; `docs/config.md:13,519` already record that reader as REMOVED in favour of `rebar.toml` / a `[tool.rebar]` pyproject table.\n- **Stale mypy comment**: `pyproject.toml:488-490` says the non-core tree \"is checked advisory-only for now,\" but CI GATES mypy over the whole library (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` \"GATING: mypy over the WHOLE library AND scripts/\", and `Makefile:248` `typecheck: ## ... mypy over the whole library + scripts/ (gating)`).\n\n## Approach\nCorrect each drifted example/label/comment against the CURRENT contract; no behavior change.\n- In the two quickstart claim examples (`README.md:44`, `docs/user-guide.md:115`) **omit `--assignee` entirely** — `claim` then applies the configured `ticket.default_assignee` (`docs/config.md:466`), which is the behaviour AGENTS.md tells agents to use. Same for the adjacent library line `README.md:50` → `rebar.claim(tid)`. Adjust the trailing alignment comment on `README.md:44` so the fence stays tidy.\n- Where an assignee value is genuinely illustrative (`docs/user-guide.md:234`, the `rebar edit` field example) substitute an email form (`--assignee=alice@example.com`) that IS Jira-resolvable, and add a one-clause note in the surrounding prose pointing at `config.md`'s Jira-resolvable requirement.\n- `docs/README.md:25` → link `mcp-reference.md` (keeping `llm-framework.md` mentioned for the agent/gate operations, so no index entry is orphaned).\n- `docs/README.md:91` → describe `config.md` as `rebar.toml` / `[tool.rebar]` keys, precedence, and design of record.\n- `pyproject.toml:488-490` → state that mypy is gated over the whole library and `scripts/`, with `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` layering the extra `disallow_untyped_defs` ratchet on the promoted packages.\n\n## Scope (docs + one TOML comment only)\n- `README.md` — quickstart claim example (44) and the adjacent library example (50).\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — claim example (115) and `edit` example (234) + one clause of surrounding prose.\n- `docs/README.md` — MCP route (25) and the `config.md` description (91).\n- `pyproject.toml` — the `[tool.mypy]` header comment (488-490). No `[tool.mypy]` VALUES change; the ratchet-flip is explicitly out of scope (pyproject.toml is contended, per the epic).\n- NOT changed: `docs/identity.md:184` (legitimately cites legacy `.rebar/config.conf` as a per-machine override), `docs/release-notes.md:361` (historical removal record), `docs/cli-reference.md` (GENERATED from CLI help — its `--assignee` strings are option syntax, not a value example), `docs/exit-codes.md:78` / `README.md:345` (`<you>` placeholders, not bare handles).\n\n## Risk / generator + gate interactions\n- None of the four edited files are generator-owned (the generators are `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `gen_mcp_reference.py`, `gen_env_registry.py`, `gen_adr_index.py`, targeting `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/env-vars.md`, the ADR index — none in scope).\n- `scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` EXTRACTS and EXECUTES the README `## Quickstart` bash block in CI; `tests/scripts/test_check_readme_quickstart.py::test_extract_real_readme_has_golden_path_commands` asserts it still contains `rebar init` / `rebar create` / `rebar claim` / `rebar transition`. Dropping only the `--assignee alice` argument keeps all four needles and keeps the block runnable (`claim` without `--assignee` is the documented default path), so both stay green. That test's other `--assignee alice` occurrences are its OWN synthetic fixtures and are not touched.\n- `scripts/check_docs_index.py` checks docs-index completeness and dead links: changing `docs/README.md:25`'s target from `llm-framework.md` to `mcp-reference.md` keeps both files indexed elsewhere (`llm-framework.md` and `mcp-reference.md` each retain their own index entries), so no file becomes unindexed and no link becomes dead.\n\n## Verification\n- Docs/comment-only: no `src/rebar/**` and no test-behavior changes; the existing docs/link/golden gates stay green.\n- Full local gate set before push: the ten `scripts/check_*` gates, generator no-diff vs `git archive HEAD`, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the CI test selection `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"`.\n- Each corrected truth is confirmed by a grep assertion below rather than by manual reading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No quickstart/user-guide example teaches a Jira-unresolvable bare handle: `grep -rnE '\\-\\-assignee[= ]+[A-Za-z]+([^@A-Za-z]|$)' README.md docs/user-guide.md` returns nothing, and `grep -n 'assignee=\"alice\"' README.md` returns nothing.\n- [x] `grep -n 'Drive rebar over MCP' -A1 docs/README.md` links `mcp-reference.md`, and `grep -n 'config\\.conf' docs/README.md` returns nothing.\n- [x] `grep -n 'advisory-only for now' pyproject.toml` returns nothing and the `[tool.mypy]` header comment names whole-library (+`scripts/`) gating; `git diff pyproject.toml` shows comment lines only (no key/value change).\n- [x] `git diff --name-only origin/main` lists exactly `README.md`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `pyproject.toml` — no `src/rebar/**`, no `tests/**`.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py`, `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` all pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786619445568181001,"uuid":"13a2b61c-5350-4d4d-9bb8-0698c7542778"}